WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.623
Every chlorine atom has a
mass number of thirty-five or

2
00:00:03.673 --> 00:00:04.770
thirty-seven.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.050
Whole numbers, every time.

4
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.170
Yet look up chlorine
in the periodic table,

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.370
and its relative atomic mass
is thirty-five point five.

6
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.070
No single chlorine atom
anywhere has that mass.

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.990
So where does thirty-five
point five come from?

8
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.510
In this mission, you'll
meet the protons,

9
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.870
neutrons and electrons inside an atom,

10
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.310
and learn what the atomic number
and the mass number tell you.

11
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.350
You'll discover isotopes,

12
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.890
atoms of the same element
with different masses,

13
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.690
and find out how a relative
atomic mass is worked out.

14
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.210
Your mission: explain why chlorine
is thirty-five point five.
